    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-11, ONE entry, gate-side-only: agent/tools/provider/mailbox-banner.ts 58 -> 127 for UX-REPAIR T39 (`a1da94a`), argued in that commit. +47 code / +44 comment against -20 code: the file gained the AGENT half of a rule that had only ever had its user half, which is the defect the owner reported, plus the resolver call that makes the header name the mailbox that was actually served. Same hand-move discipline as the T37 entry above and for the same reason — a blanket --record would reset 28 other files' headroom silently.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-11, ONE entry, gate-side-only: plaud/auth.ts 278 -> 351 for UX-REPAIR T38 (`4c7a908`), argued in that commit. +27 code / +51 comment against -5 code: the file gained the ONE owner of the Plaud expiry transition — the thing whose absence is the owner's report — and `refreshPlaudAccountInfo`'s duplicate of that state change was folded into it. Same hand-move discipline as the T37 and T39 entries above and for the same reason.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: engine-riders.ts 109 -> 185 for HARNESS-LEARNINGS HL4 step 2 (2c). +16 code / +60 comment: the code is `QUEUE_PAIRED_RIDERS`, the declaration of the SECOND steering channel the census called “THE BIG ONE” — seven floors (not the inherited six) that write their steer's text to the events lane as well as the queue, each with its declared latch and its rider intent. The comment half is the measurement that says why the seven writes STAY (the queue is per-turn state; the rider is the only carrier that survives into the next turn) and the design call that is handed up rather than taken in a governance commit. Moved BY HAND rather than by --record, the discipline the three 2026-08-11 entries above set and for their reason: a blanket re-record would silently reset the headroom of every other file that has drifted since 36fe2fe and is still under the limit. recordedAt/recordedAtCommit are deliberately NOT touched.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: no-tool-calls.ts 71 -> 104 for HARNESS-LEARNINGS HL4 step 2 (2a). The CODE SHRANK, 47 -> 44: the hand-written seven-call sequence became a table-sorted list and a five-line loop. The growth is entirely the declaration and its argument — which of the four orderings is the authority, and the `going-idle` inversion that starved two owed-person floors until this commit. Moved BY HAND rather than by --record, the discipline the three 2026-08-11 entries above set and for their reason: a blanket re-record would silently reset the headroom of every other file that has drifted since 36fe2fe and is still under the limit. recordedAt/recordedAtCommit are deliberately NOT touched.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: work/obligation-memory.ts 448 -> 619 for UX-REPAIR ROUND 11 T44, argued in ratchets.json's $raises (556 -> 619) and in that commit. The baseline entry is the 2026-08-10 448 and the ratchet pin was the later 556, so this move carries HL5's and HL6's recorded raises as well as T44's — both numbers are moved, and both by hand. T44's own +63 is 22 code (the `BoardCounts` shape, one tracker-rows predicate taken from `tracker-view.ts`, one four-count statement) and 37 comment: the module gained §7, the count reader for the rest of the board, beside §5's set reader, because \"what does the spine say is outstanding\" keeps one owner. Moved BY HAND rather than by --record, the discipline the 2026-08-11 entries above set and for their reason, with one more this sitting: a second builder is working in this same tree, and a blanket re-record would silently absorb THEIR growth into this commit. recordedAt/recordedAtCommit are deliberately NOT touched.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: memory/recall-lane.ts 547 -> 708 for UX-REPAIR ROUND 11 T44, argued in ratchets.json's $raises (665 -> 708) and in that commit. As above, the baseline entry predates HL5's recorded raise, so this move carries 547 -> 665 -> 708. T44's own +43 is 17 code (the `board` payload field, the exported line builder, the read taken beside the commitment set, the worst-case term) and 30 comment, less the four lines the snapshot renderer's signature and returns replaced. Same hand-move discipline and the same concurrent-builder reason.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: agent/tools/cat/web.ts 68 -> 107 for UX-REPAIR ROUND 11 T45. The file is unpinned in ratchets.json (107 is well under maxNewFileLines) so the growth detector is the only gate that sees it, which is what it is for. +39: 4 code (one exported literal, one three-line helper, and one gated append in each of the two read handlers) and 29 of comment. The comment is a relocation-purity file's whole defence — it states which incidents bought the line (round-11 S1's unsourced market hours, S4's Denver), why it rides the tool RESULT rather than the prefix (dsh F4 / HL6's own migration), that it costs zero cached bytes, and why a refusal is returned byte-identical. Same hand-move discipline and the same concurrent-builder reason.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: finalize-record.ts 337 -> 430 for HARNESS-LEARNINGS HL4 step 2 (the non-delivery record). +30 code / +63 comment against the HL3-era 378: the code is one reader for “written, never seen by the model”, HL3's mirror, in the same shape as the T41 rider beside it. Note the baseline entry is the 2026-08-10 337 and the ratchet pin is the later 378 — both are moved, and both are moved by hand. Moved BY HAND rather than by --record, the discipline the three 2026-08-11 entries above set and for their reason: a blanket re-record would silently reset the headroom of every other file that has drifted since 36fe2fe and is still under the limit. recordedAt/recordedAtCommit are deliberately NOT touched.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-15, ONE entry, gate-side-only: agent/v2/steps/finalize/close-the-loop.ts 94 -> 158 for UX-REPAIR ROUND 11 T42 (the completion report stops re-announcing an answer the owner already has), argued file-by-file in ratchets.json's $raises and in that commit. +12 code / +52 comment: the code is one import, a two-entry constant, a 10-line SQL helper and one `AND NOT` in the selector; the comment is the ledger rows that prove the defect (task 34519aca closed 01:28:33, its receipt 1f03db51 delivered to the owner at 01:25:51) plus the two MEASUREMENTS a reader cannot re-derive from the code — `work.conversation_id` is NULL on every task row on the dev body (which is why the guard scopes by channel, not conversation) and 125 `done` one-shot rows point their receipt at a `tool-turn` chip (which is why the chip clause exists at all; without it the guard would suppress reports that really are owed). The better home for the predicate is beside its sibling `turnDeliveredToPerson` in `answered-edge.ts`, which is outside this worker's fence and is recorded as a hand-up rather than taken. Moved BY HAND rather than by --record, the discipline the 2026-08-11 entries set and for their reason: a blanket re-record silently resets the headroom of every other file that has drifted since 36fe2fe and is still under the limit. A second builder (W31) is in this same tree this sitting, which is a second reason. recordedAt/recordedAtCommit are deliberately NOT touched.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-16, ONE entry, gate-side-only: prompt/templates.ts 119 -> 186 for UX-REPAIR ROUND 12 T59 (W42), the service agents' souls. This file IS the in-code last-resort defaults module (DEFAULT_SOUL_MD, DEFAULT_PM_SOUL_MD, DEFAULT_TRAINER_SOUL_MD already live here), and T59 moved two more into it: the Healer's and the Imaginer's fallbacks, lifted out of `healer/healer-agent.ts` and `imaginer/imaginer-agent.ts` when their dead template readers were deleted. +66 is 55 of doctrine STRING that already existed elsewhere in the tree and 11 of comment; the two source files fell 51 and 23 lines in the same commit, so the tree is net SHORTER across the move. One change of substance in the moved bytes, declared: the Imaginer's stub interpolated `${imaginerName}` through its own private substituter and now carries `{{imaginer_agent_name}}` for the ONE substituter to fill — an in-code default that fills names its own way is the second-writer defect W24 and W25 each spent a task closing. `--record` was REFUSED, per the T37-T40 precedent above: a blanket re-record would reset the headroom of every other file that has drifted since 36fe2fe, and nobody else's slack is mine to spend.",
    "HAND-MOVED, 2026-08-16, ONE entry, gate-side-only: prompt/assembler.ts 1458 -> 1823 for UX-REPAIR ROUND 13 T61(a) (W43), the unsourced-specifics conduct sentence, argued in ratchets.json's $raises (1787 -> 1823) and in that commit. The baseline entry is the 2026-08-10 1458 and the ratchet pin was the later 1787, so this move carries T59's recorded raise (1691 -> 1787) as well as T61's own +36 — both numbers are moved, and both by hand. T61(a) itself is 4 code lines (one section pushed into sys.tools) and 30 of comment, and the comment is the load-bearing half: the plan REQUIRES the honest bound recorded where the rule is written — that this is the weak surface by our own HL6 evidence and that the measurement half lives at teardown/finalize-record.ts — because without it the next reader either trusts the sentence to have fixed the class or deletes it as decoration. This file is the ONE owner of soul resolution (T40) and of the engine-owned conduct sentences (T23), which is why three of the last four rounds have landed here by construction rather than by sprawl. `--record` was REFUSED, per the T37-T40 and T59 precedents above: a blanket re-record would reset the headroom of every other file that has drifted since 36fe2fe, and nobody else's slack is mine to spend. recordedAt/recordedAtCommit are deliberately NOT touched.",
